Where the boot thread and the matching thread are

The panel of run 555 ends with the console's last line and not one of
bsd_init's phases, even though those phases are written to the panel before
they are written to the console.  So the boot thread never reached the first
phase of bsd_init, and nothing on the panel says where.

The beacon is the one that can carry it.  The heartbeat uses delay(), which
needs timers that are not running yet, so it prints HB 1 and stops -- its own
patch says so -- and run 556 put the waypoint there and the panel showed
nothing.  Run 560 wrote it once a second and the panel showed nothing
either: the clock does not tick yet at this point of the boot, so
clock_get_uptime() returns zero, which is the same reason the heartbeat's
delay() never returns.  The beacon counts its own marks and writes the
waypoint every fourth one.

Run 561 said w8: the boot thread is between vm_set_restrictions() and
bsd_init().  The only thing there is kperf_init_early(), whose first act is
ml_wait_max_cpus() -- a wait for every CPU to be accounted for.  Only IOKit
publishes that count: ml_set_max_cpus() is called from AppleARMSMP and from
IOCPU, and only a personality that was probed and attached calls either.  So
the boot thread waits for the matching, and the matching has to finish --
and it has not: no candidate ever reaches its probe.

So the matching thread gets a waypoint too, and the beacon writes both.

The boot thread:

   1  after the oslog startup functions
   2  after the mach ipc startup functions
   3  after the thread call startup functions
   4  after the sysctl startup functions
   5  after the early boot startup functions
   6  after the lockdown startup functions
   7  after the IOKit lockdown, before vm_set_restrictions()
   8  after vm_set_restrictions()
   9  at the call of bsd_init()
  10  at the top of bsd_init(), before boot_progress_stage()
  11  after boot_progress_stage()
  12  after platform_stall_panic_or_spin()
  13  after throttle_init()
  14  after the copyright is printed

The matching thread:

   1  running PE_lockdown_iokit()
   2  PE_lockdown_iokit() returned
   3  probeCandidates was entered
   4  about to call inst->probe()
   5  inst->probe() returned

